messages:
jess: quick check — we're seeing clients cancel an ongoing streaming generation (Node AbortController) but the server keeps sending tokens for ~2s and billing/metrics still attribute it. Any recommendations for consistent cancel semantics across node/python/go?

mike: ugh yeah. observed that too with retry middleware. abort stops the app loop but the retry layer re-issues reqs unless we short-circuit it. in node we hook AbortSignal in the retry layer to throw immediately. use `if (signal.aborted) throw new AbortError()` before retry.

sam: python note: async `timeout` wrappers (e.g., anyio/asyncio.wait_for) will cancel the coroutine but aiohttp may still have a socket read in progress. we call `client.close()` on cancel to force the connection closed. also expose a `CancelledError` type from the sdk to unify handling.

alexa: go: context cancellation should cascade. our issue was we spawn goroutines for streaming and don't select on `ctx.Done()` in the write loop. add `select { case <-ctx.Done(): return ctx.Err(); default: }` in send/recv loops.

chandra: streaming quirk — server-side buffers + http/2 flow control can cause extra tokens after cancel was acknowledged. we mitigated by: 1) send a cancel signal to control-plane to stop generation asap, 2) close transport from client side, 3) mark the call in telemetry as cancelled so billing pipeline can prorate.

mike: practical pattern we landed on: (1) top-level cancel API that sets an atomic flag, (2) all retry/backoff code checks flag before attempting request, (3) in-flight request still listens to AbortSignal/context and triggers transport close, (4) SDK returns a canonical `sdk.Cancelled` error.

jess: can we share small code snippets for each language to copy into SDK? will add to docs.

mike: node example: ```js
// caller
const ac = new AbortController();
client.generate({ ... , signal: ac.signal });
// cancel later
ac.abort();
// in SDK retry loop
if (signal?.aborted) throw new Error('Cancelled');
// when making fetch: fetch(url, { signal }) // native aborts socket
```

sam: python example: ```py
# caller
with anyio.fail_after(5):
    await client.generate(...)
# SDK
if cancel_event.is_set():
    raise SDKCancelledError()
# when transport active
await transport.aclose()  # force close on cancel
```

chandra: go example: ```go
ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(parentCtx, 5*time.Second)
defer cancel()
err := client.Generate(ctx, opts)
// inside streaming loop
select {
case <-ctx.Done(): return ctx.Err()
case chunk := <-recv: // handle
}
```

alexa: ops note — we should also add a test harness that simulates mid-stream cancel + server-side slow drain to assert SDK surfaces cancel quickly and we don't spin retries. can pair with @mike tomorrow. :calendar:

devex-bot: Added `devex/timeout-cancel-guidelines` doc to the team drive (draft). Please review.

jess: awesome, thanks. I'll take docs + examples and open a PR with a checklist: retry short-circuit, transport-close, canonical error, telemetry tag (cancelled). pinging @mike @sam for review. :rocket:
